---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout title={SITE.name}>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <h1 class="name">Anandu Ramachandran</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">{SITE.tags.join(' · ')}</p>

    <p class="statement">
      Somewhere between learning technology, reading{' '}
      <em>too much history</em>, and chasing philosophical rabbit holes
      online, mostly looking for good ideas in between.
    </p>

    <div class="intro">
      <p>Hey, I’m Anandu.</p>

      <p>
        I’m a software developer who enjoys being around technology and
        learning how things work. It’s something I’ve always wanted to build
        my life around, and I still enjoy discovering new ideas, solving
        problems, and figuring out how to make things work a little better.
      </p>

      <p>
        Outside of work, I’m usually somewhere between a book, a movie, or an
        unnecessarily long rabbit hole about history and philosophy. I love
        reading and getting completely absorbed in a good book. I also really
        enjoy movies. A genuinely good movie can make my day a lot better,
        even if the day wasn’t going particularly well to begin with.
      </p>

      <p>
        I’m also a huge anime fan, with One Piece holding a particularly
        special place in my heart. There’s something about getting invested
        in a story and its characters over hundreds of episodes that I really
        love. And yes, I will probably talk about One Piece if you give me
        the opportunity.
      </p>

      <p>
        I love travelling too, especially the idea of experiencing different
        cultures, food, people, and ways of life. I don’t get to travel
        nearly as often as I’d like, but it’s something I hope to do a lot
        more of.
      </p>

      <p>
        The idea for this website actually came from one of my college
        seniors. He once described his own website as “a selfish pursuit of
        storing and curating knowledge”, a place to collect his ideas and the
        things he found interesting or inspiring. He also described it as a
        living record of his learnings, built on the idea that we change as
        we continue to learn new things.
      </p>

      <p>
        That idea stuck with me. A lot of the elements and the overall feel
        of this site are inspired by his work, so I owe him credit for giving
        me the idea to start this in the first place. This is my own version
        of that idea, a place where I can keep track of the things I read,
        learn, think about, and find interesting.
      </p>

      <p>
        It’s not meant to be a perfect representation of who I am. It’s just
        a little record of what has caught my attention along the way.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you happen to enjoy books, movies, anime, history, technology, or
        the occasional philosophical rabbit hole, I’d be happy to have you
        around. Maybe you’ll find something here that makes you curious
        about something new.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-block: var(--space-7) var(--space-8);
  }

  .name {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6.5vw, 4rem);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    max-width: 18ch;
  }

  .subtitle {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
  }

  .statement {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.4vw, 2.4rem);
    line-height: 1.35;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
    max-width: 26ch;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .intro {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    max-width: var(--content-max);
  }

  .intro p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .intro p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
